# Applies to `vercel` CLI deployments only — a Git deploy clones the whole repo
# and ignores this file. The CLI reads this file INSTEAD of .gitignore, so
# anything that should stay out of an upload has to be listed here.
#
# Note what is deliberately NOT listed: site/.
#
#   * Git deploy   — site/ is git-ignored, so Vercel never receives it and
#                    vercel.json builds the docs with MkDocs.
#   * CLI deploy   — if the machine running `vercel` has a locally built site/,
#                    it IS uploaded, and vercel.json publishes it as-is instead
#                    of building. That is the "no Python needed" path.

.git
.github
.obsidian

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.cache/

# The original flat note folders, superseded by docs/. ~4.9 MB the build never
# reads — they stay in the repo for history, but there is no reason to upload
# them on every deploy.
01-Server/
02-Systemd/
03-Handle-Can/
04-YOCTO/
06-PortingFreeRtos/
07-Unit-Test/
08-DBus/
09-NetwokManagement/
10-SIM-Module/
11-CarHw/
GUI/
Images/
